CORE
read.c
--isr isr
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 11 the handler may run before a read: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 12 the handler need not run before a read: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
main only reads x, which the handler writes: the handler may run before that
read. The assignment to other, which the handler does not access, gets no call.
